{# /get-started, a CUSTOM conversion page (no page template). This is the endpoint
   every built page's CTA links to, so it composes the library macros directly on
   base.njk. Schema is BreadcrumbList ONLY, per the build instruction: it's an action
   page, not a Service or Person entity. The light FAQ is rendered VISIBLY but WITHOUT
   FAQPage schema, to honor "just BreadcrumbList" and to leave the canonical FAQPage
   entity to the dedicated /faq page (no competing FAQPage nodes).

   Gold discipline: the two gold moments (the hero booking button and the closing
   booking band) both point at the real Calendly scheduler and sit in separate
   viewports. Booking goes straight to site.booking.calendlyUrl (we are already ON
   /get-started, so the CTA is the actual scheduler, not the getStartedPath). Fees
   are surfaced BEFORE the call per the DNA instruction, using confirmed CLIENT_FACTS
   ranges (a /fees page does not exist yet, so ranges are stated inline, not linked).
   All facts come from site data. No em dashes. #}
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}
{% import "components/sections.njk" as s %}
{% set faqResolvedItems = faq | resolveFaq(faqEntries) %}

{{ s.breadcrumbs(crumbs) }}

{{ s.hero({
  eyebrow: "Get started",
  title: "Getting started is one",
  titleEmphasis: "low-pressure call.",
  variant: "center",
  lead: "It begins with a free 15 to 20 minute Get to Know Us call. No intake interrogation, no commitment, just a chance to tell us what's going on and see whether we're the right fit. Ready when you are.",
  cta: { href: "#book", label: "Book your free call", gold: true }
}) }}

{{ s.steps({
  eyebrow: "What happens on the call",
  title: "Four small steps, and none of them are scary",
  lead: "Reaching out is the part people dread most. Here's exactly how it goes, so nothing about it is a surprise.",
  steps: [
    { title: "You book the free call", body: "Pick a time that works on our scheduler. It's 15 to 20 minutes, by phone or video, and it's genuinely free. You don't need to prepare anything or have your story tidy." },
    { title: "We listen", body: "You tell us what's bringing you in, in your own words and at your own pace. We're listening for what you need and hoping you'll feel understood, not running you through a checklist." },
    { title: "We match you to the right person", body: "Based on what you share, we point you to the right therapist, whether that's Kay directly or one of the associates she personally trains and supervises. The fit matters more than the resume." },
    { title: "You book your first session", body: "If it feels right, we schedule your first full session with that therapist, usually within 24 hours. If we're not the right fit, we'll happily point you toward someone who is." }
  ]
}) }}

{#
  THE ROOM, placed between the steps and the scheduler. The single biggest thing
  standing between someone reading this page and booking is not information, it is
  the unknown of walking into a stranger's office. Showing the actual room, which
  is modest and looks like a living room rather than a clinic, answers that better
  than another paragraph would. Real photograph of the practice (IMAGE_MANIFEST.md),
  never a stock or AI interior.
#}
{{ s.promoCallout({
  tone: "seafoam",
  eyebrow: "Where it happens",
  title: "The room you'd actually",
  titleEmphasis: "walk into.",
  body: [
    "No clipboard clinic, no waiting room with a sliding glass window. Our office on Third Street looks a lot more like someone's living room, because an hour spent talking about the hardest thing in your life should not also involve fluorescent lighting.",
    "If getting here is the hard part, telehealth covers any California resident, and Beach Therapy happens on the coastline a few blocks away. The room is one option of three."
  ],
  href: "/contact",
  label: "Find the office",
  image: {
    src: "https://cdn.circulationstudio.com/clients/laguna-beach-counseling/interior/laguna-beach-counseling-office-interior-6.webp",
    alt: "A session room at the practice seen from the doorway, an orange sofa and armchairs around a woven coffee table, table lamps lit and framed landscapes on the wall."
  }
}) }}

{#
  THE SCHEDULER. This is the page every CTA on the site points at, so booking
  belongs on it rather than one more click away. Placed after the four steps: the
  reader now knows what the call is, so this is the moment to pick a time.
  The hero's gold button was pointing at calendly.com and now points at #book,
  because sending someone off-site when the scheduler is right here is the worse
  of the two experiences. The closing band still links out, as a fallback for
  anyone who reached the bottom without booking.
#}
{{ s.calendlyEmbed({
  id: "book",
  tone: "sand",
  eyebrow: "Pick a time",
  title: "Book your free",
  titleEmphasis: "Get to Know Us call.",
  lead: "Choose whatever slot suits you. It is 15 to 20 minutes, by phone or video, and nothing is owed after it.",
  url: site.booking.calendlyUrl + "?" + site.booking.embedParams,
  note: "Booking is handled by Calendly. Please keep anything sensitive off the booking form; we will cover it on the call."
}) }}

{# NOTE (flagged, not yet actioned): /fees now exists and carries the full rate cards
   plus the out-of-network reasoning and Superbill detail. These inline ranges could
   become a link to /fees instead of (or alongside) the summary table here. Left
   unchanged pending confirmation, per the build instruction not to auto-change
   get-started. #}
{{ s.rateTable({
  caption: "What sessions cost, before you ever get on the call",
  rows: [
    { service: "Sessions with an associate therapist", rate: "$160 to $315" },
    { service: "Sessions with Kay Wenger", rate: "$190 to $390" }
  ],
  footnote: "The range reflects session length (50, 75, or 90 minutes) and format (individual, couples, or family). We're out-of-network and provide a Superbill at every session for PPO reimbursement. A sliding scale is available on request. The free Get to Know Us call is always free."
}) }}

{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>Why don't we take insurance directly? {{ site.positioning.outOfNetworkLine }}</p>
  <p>Wondering if that's worth it? For a lot of people it is, and if cost is the thing standing between you and starting, say so on the call. That's a conversation, not a closed door.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% if faq.tags or faq.items %}{{ s.faq({ eyebrow: faq.eyebrow, title: faq.title, items: faqResolvedItems }) }}{% endif %}

